{%- endcase -%}
{%- assign CATK = 'materials,maintenance,posts,northkit,vlog' -%}
{%- comment -%}
 ?? Configuration ?????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????
 BITC_BLOG handle of the blog that carries the series. Used when the page is not
 a blog template (the hub is a normal page and has no `blog` object).
 The live store's general blog is `novinky`; the series gets its own blog
 because a Liquid loop over `blog.articles` stops at the newest 50, and
 Novinky already holds ~25 material entries and keeps growing — chapter
 articles would eventually fall out of the hub's reach.
 BITC_SERIES series tag, used only when the series shares a blog with other content.
 Leave empty when the series has its own blog (the recommended setup).
 CH_TAGS chapter tags, in order. An article belongs to a chapter by carrying its
 tag; a chapter with no published article renders as "coming soon".
 CH_NAMES chapter names. Proper names and product lines stay in English in every
 market (Katka, Peak Flow); only the subtitles are translated (t_chNsub).
 PER cards per page in the archive grid.
 FEATURED article handles, in the order they should appear at the top. Shopify orders
 a blog by publish date only, so an import buried the editorial writing under
 eighty material entries. This list is read by handle, so it reaches an
 article at any depth — a tag would only reach the newest fifty — and the
 order is exactly the order written here. The first four fill the band; the
 rest open the grid on page one. An unknown handle is skipped in silence.
 SHOW_READ_TIME off while most articles keep their text in an EComposer template
 rather than in `article.content` — the number would be missing on some
 cards and present on others. Turn it on once the bodies or the
 `read_time` metafields are filled in.
 ??????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign BITC_BLOG = 'novinky' -%}
{%- assign BITC_SERIES = '' -%}
{%- assign BITC_HUB = '/pages/born-in-the-carpathians' -%}
{%- assign CH_TAGS = 'chapter-01,chapter-02,chapter-03,chapter-04' -%}
{%- assign CH_NAMES = 'Katka & Shoes|David & Peak Flow|Skialp|Backpacks' -%}
{%- assign PER = 12 -%}
{%- assign FEATURED = 'ako-vznikaju-topanky-northfinder,sk-top-10-kratkych-mestskych-tur-na-slovensku-pre-tych-co-potre,sk-northfinder-volbou-slovenskych-outdooristov-ziskali-sme-ocen,sk-meru-a-makalu-topanky-ktore-presli-svet,sk-northfinder-draci-a-dracia-vasen-nova-oblubena-skrysa-pred-da,sk-nemali-by-ste-dychat-len-vy-ale-aj-vase-oblecenie,sk-jarna-kolekcia-northfinder-nalahko-neznamena-lahkovazne,sk-neda-sa-vidiet-neda-sa-kupit-priatelstvo-je-ta-najkrajsia-ve,sk-ako-sa-obliect-na-horsku-turistiku,sl-gabriel-baicus-obleka-mora-biti-partner-na-katerega-se-l' -%}
{%- assign SHOW_READ_TIME = false -%}
{%- comment -%}
 `blog` exists on a blog template. On the hub page it is nil, so the handle is read
 from the path — the segment after /blogs/, which survives a locale prefix like /de/ —
 and only then does it fall back to BITC_BLOG.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign bitc_blog = blog -%}
{%- if bitc_blog == blank -%}
 {%- assign bitc_bh = request.path | split: '/blogs/' | last | split: '/' | first -%}
 {%- if blogs[bitc_bh] != blank -%}{%- assign bitc_blog = blogs[bitc_bh] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if bitc_blog == blank -%}{%- assign bitc_blog = blogs[BITC_BLOG] -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
 Where the series shares a blog, the archive lives at the series tag URL and every
 "all articles" link has to keep that filter on.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign bitc_all_url = bitc_blog.url -%}
{%- assign bitc_tag_prefix = bitc_blog.url | append: '/tagged/' -%}
{%- if BITC_SERIES != blank -%}
 {%- assign bitc_all_url = bitc_blog.url | append: '/tagged/' | append: BITC_SERIES -%}
 {%- assign bitc_tag_prefix = bitc_all_url | append: '+' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
 The series tag is the floor of this view, not a filter on it — so it never counts as
 the active topic and never shows up as one of the pills.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign feat_h = FEATURED | split: ',' -%}
{%- assign FEATURED_C = ',' | append: FEATURED | append: ',' -%}
{%- assign bitc_tag = blank -%}
{%- for tg in current_tags -%}
 {%- assign tgh = tg | handle -%}
 {%- if tgh != BITC_SERIES -%}{%- assign bitc_tag = tg -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign bitc_tagh = bitc_tag | handle -%}
{%- comment -%}
 Hidden when a chapter or topic filter is on: a filtered view should be one honest
 list, not a fixed band above a filtered grid.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign bitc_n = bitc_blog.articles_count | default: 0 -%}
{%- paginate bitc_blog.articles by PER -%}
{%- if bitc_tag == blank and bitc_n > 1 and paginate.current_page == 1 -%}
<style>
/* ?? Northfinder design-manual tokens. Every value here is from the manual or
 marked [derived]. No #000, no grey outside the Carbon tints, no pills,
 no shadows, Montserrat in Medium 500 and Bold 700 only. ????????????????? */
.nfb,.nfb *,.nfb *::before,.nfb *::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
.nfb{width:100vw;position:relative;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);overflow-x:clip;background:#FFFFFF;
 --ink:#2B3C48; /* Carbon — all body and heading text */
 --ink-80:#556370; /* [derived] Carbon 80% — meta TEXT. Carbon 60% measures 2.9:1
 on white and fails WCAG AA for normal text, so text never
 uses it; this tint measures 6.1:1. */
 --ink-60:#808A91; /* Carbon 60% — lines, icons, disabled chrome. Never text. */
 --line:#D5D8DA; /* Carbon 20% — 1px dividers, surfaces */
 --red:#E3350E; /* Northfinder Red — large fills only */
 --red-ink:#C72D0C; /* [derived] small red text and 14px button fills, 5.5:1 */
 --red-hover:#AD270A; /* [derived] */
 --red-20:#F9D7CF;
 --r:4px;--r-sm:2px;--r-lg:8px;
 --gutter:48px;--sec-y:96px;--band-y:56px;--block-y:32px;--wrap:1440px;
 --ease:cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1);
 font-family:'Montserrat',system-ui,-apple-system,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;
 font-weight:500;font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink);
 -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;text-rendering:optimizeLegibility}
@media(max-width:1199px){.nfb{--gutter:32px;--sec-y:72px;--band-y:48px}}
@media(max-width:767px){.nfb{--gutter:20px;--sec-y:56px;--band-y:36px;--block-y:24px}}
.nfb[hidden]{display:none}
.nfb img{display:block;max-width:100%}
.nfb a,.nfb a:visited,.nfb a:hover,.nfb a:active{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}
.nfb button{font:inherit;color:inherit;background:none;border:0;padding:0;cursor:pointer}
/* the UA maps <b> to `bolder`, which resolves to 900 inside a 700 parent — the manual
 loads Medium and Bold only, so pin it */
.nfb b,.nfb strong{font-weight:700}
.nfb ._w{max-width:var(--wrap);margin:0 auto;padding:0 var(--gutter)}
/* type roles — manual's hierarchy, rebased for running text */
.nfb ._eyebrow{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
.nfb ._h1{font-size:clamp(28px,20px + 1.1vw,40px);font-weight:700;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:0}
.nfb ._h2{font-size:clamp(20px,17px + .35vw,24px);font-weight:700;line-height:1.25}
.nfb ._body{font-size:16px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.6;max-width:70ch}
/* A last line holding one short word reads as a mistake. `balance` evens out short
 blocks — headings and standfirsts — and `pretty` keeps running text from ending on a
 lone word. Both are progressive: a browser without them simply wraps as before. */
.nfb ._h1,.nfb ._h2,.nfb ._eyebrow{text-wrap:balance}
.nfb ._small{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5}
@media(max-width:767px){.nfb ._eyebrow{font-size:12px}}
/* buttons — 4px radius, no pills, flat. Primary rests on the derived red so the
 14px uppercase label clears 4.5:1. */
.nfb ._btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;height:48px;padding:0 24px;
 border-radius:var(--r);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;
 transition:background-color .18s var(--ease),color .18s var(--ease),border-color .18s var(--ease)}
.nfb ._btn._pri{background:var(--red-ink);color:#FFFFFF}
.nfb ._btn._pri:hover{background:var(--red-hover)}
.nfb ._btn._sec{background:#FFFFFF;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--ink)}
.nfb ._btn._sec:hover{background:var(--ink);color:#FFFFFF}
@media(max-width:767px){.nfb ._btn{height:52px;width:100%}}
/* image placeholder — a post with no cover must not collapse the grid */
.nfb ._ph{position:relative;background:var(--line);overflow:hidden}
.nfb ._ph::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background-image:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,rgba(43,60,72,.06) 0 10px,rgba(43,60,72,0) 10px 20px)}
.nfb ._ph::after{content:attr(data-ph);position:absolute;left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);
 font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-80);white-space:nowrap}
.nfb ._sr{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}
.nfb a:focus-visible,.nfb button:focus-visible,.nfb input:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ink);outline-offset:2px}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.nfb *,.nfb *::before,.nfb *::after{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}}
/* ?? shared card atoms (episode card, compact row, filter control) ????????????? */
.nfb ._chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:24px;padding:0 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);
 border-radius:var(--r-sm);background:#FFFFFF;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;
 text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink);white-space:nowrap}
.nfb ._chip._on{background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);color:#FFFFFF}
.nfb ._meta{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--ink-80)}
.nfb ._meta ._bar{width:1px;height:12px;background:var(--line);flex:0 0 auto}
/* square, never circular — the manual allows no circular badges but the symbol lockup */
.nfb ._more{flex:0 0 auto;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;
 letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red-ink);white-space:nowrap}
.nfb ._more svg{transition:transform .18s var(--ease)}
.nfb ._card:hover ._more{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px}
.nfb ._card:hover ._more svg{transform:translateX(3px)}
.nfb ._play{position:absolute;left:16px;bottom:16px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:32px;padding:0 12px;
 border-radius:var(--r);background:var(--red);color:#FFFFFF;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase}
.nfb ._card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%}
.nfb ._card ._shot{position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--r);background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line)}
/* A small or banner-shaped source cannot fill a 16:10 box without being destroyed. The
 store's featured images are banners on white, so the box is white too and the picture
 simply sits in it, sharp and whole. The 1px Carbon-20 frame (on every card, not only
 these) is what keeps it anchored — the manual composes with lines, not shadows. */
.nfb ._card ._shot._fit{background:#FFFFFF}
.nfb ._card ._shot._fit img{object-fit:contain;padding:6% 8%}
.nfb ._card:hover ._shot._fit img{transform:none}
.nfb ._card ._shot img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;transition:transform .5s var(--ease)}
.nfb ._card ._shot ._ph{position:absolute;inset:0}
.nfb ._card ._shot ._chip{position:absolute;left:12px;top:12px;z-index:2;
 background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);color:#FFFFFF}
.nfb ._card ._shot ._play{z-index:2}
.nfb ._card ._ep{margin-top:16px;color:var(--ink-80)}
.nfb ._card ._ep b{color:var(--ink)}
.nfb ._card ._shot + ._h{margin-top:16px}
.nfb ._card ._h{margin-top:8px;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;text-wrap:balance;
 display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
.nfb ._card ._deck{margin-top:8px;font-size:16px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.6;text-wrap:pretty;
 display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
.nfb ._card ._foot{margin-top:auto;padding-top:16px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px}
.nfb ._card:hover ._shot img{transform:scale(1.03)}
.nfb ._card:hover ._h{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
.nfb ._lk{display:block;height:100%}
@media(max-width:767px){.nfb ._card ._h{font-size:17px}}
/* ?? LIST S2 · latest band: the newest episode large, the next three compact ??? */
.nfb._ls2{padding:var(--band-y) 0 var(--sec-y)}
.nfb._ls2 ._h2{margin-bottom:var(--block-y)}
.nfb._ls2 ._grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px}
.nfb._ls2 ._lead ._shot{aspect-ratio:16/10}
.nfb._ls2 ._lead ._h{font-size:clamp(20px,17px + .4vw,26px);-webkit-line-clamp:2}
.nfb._ls2 ._lead ._deck{-webkit-line-clamp:3}
.nfb._ls2 ._list{display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.nfb._ls2 ._row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 120px;gap:16px;align-items:center;padding:20px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.nfb._ls2 ._list ._row:first-child{padding-top:0;border-top:0}
.nfb._ls2 ._row ._rh{margin-top:8px;font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;text-wrap:balance;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
.nfb._ls2 ._row ._rd{margin-top:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5;text-wrap:pretty;color:var(--ink-80);display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
.nfb._ls2 ._row ._thumb{position:relative;aspect-ratio:4/3;border-radius:var(--r);overflow:hidden;background:var(--line)}
.nfb._ls2 ._row ._thumb img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;transition:transform .5s var(--ease)}
.nfb._ls2 ._row ._thumb ._ph{position:absolute;inset:0}
.nfb._ls2 ._row:hover ._rh{text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
.nfb._ls2 ._row:hover ._thumb img{transform:scale(1.04)}
@media(max-width:1199px){.nfb._ls2 ._grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px}._ls2 ._list ._row:first-child{padding-top:20px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}}
@media(max-width:767px){.nfb._ls2 ._row{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 96px}}
</style>
<section class="nfb _ls2" aria-labelledby="bitc-h2-latest">
 <div class="_w">
 {%- comment -%}
 One heading, no second rule under it and no "see all" button: the archive it
 pointed at is the next thing on the same page.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 <h2 class="_h2" id="bitc-h2-latest">{% if FEATURED != blank %}{{ t_featured }}{% else %}{{ t_latest }}{% endif %}</h2>
 <div class="_grid">
 {%- assign band_n = 0 -%}
 {%- if FEATURED != blank -%}
 {%- comment -%} read by handle, so depth in the blog does not matter {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- for h in feat_h -%}
 {%- capture fkey -%}{{ bitc_blog.handle }}/{{ h | strip }}{%- endcapture -%}
 {%- assign a = articles[fkey] -%}
{%- comment -%}
 One item of the band. The first becomes the lead, the next three the compact rows.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- if band_n >= 4 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- if a == blank or a.title == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- assign band_n = band_n | plus: 1 -%}
 {%- assign ep_idx = band_n -%}
 {%- comment -%} reading time, HERO video, episode number {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- comment -%}
 Articles whose body is built in EComposer keep almost nothing in
 `article.content`, so counting its words would print a confident "1 min" on a
 long read. The metafield wins when it is set; otherwise the time is computed
 only when there is a real body, and below that the line is simply left off.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- assign ep_rt = a.metafields.custom.read_time | plus: 0 -%}
 {%- if ep_rt == 0 -%}
 {%- assign ep_wc = a.content | strip_html | split: ' ' | size -%}
 {%- if ep_wc > 120 -%}
 {%- assign ep_rt = ep_wc | divided_by: 200 -%}
 {%- if ep_rt < 1 -%}{%- assign ep_rt = 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- endif -%}
 {%- endif -%}
 {%- assign ep_vid = a.metafields.custom.video_url -%}
 {%- assign ep_no = '' -%}
 {%- assign ep_inch = false -%}
 {%- for tg in a.tags -%}
 {%- assign tl = tg | handle -%}
 {%- assign tp = tl | slice: 0, 2 -%}
 {%- assign tlen = tl | size -%}
 {%- if tp == 'ep' and tlen == 4 -%}{%- assign ep_no = tl | remove_first: 'ep' -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- assign tp8 = tl | slice: 0, 8 -%}
 {%- if tp8 == 'chapter-' -%}{%- assign ep_inch = true -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- endfor -%}
 {%- comment -%}
 An article outside every chapter is not an episode: no number is invented for it
 and the episode line is left off the card entirely.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- if ep_no == blank and ep_inch -%}
 {%- if ep_idx < 10 -%}{%- assign ep_no = ep_idx | prepend: '0' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign ep_no = ep_idx -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- endif -%}
 {%- if band_n == 1 -%}
 <article class="_lead">
 <a class="_lk _card" href="{{ a.url }}">
 {%- comment -%}
 A cover only crops well when the source is big enough and roughly
 landscape. A 328x105 banner blown up into a 16:10 box is mush, so those and
 anything under 700px wide are shown whole on a Carbon-20 field instead.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- assign fit = '' -%}
 {%- if a.image and a.image.width < 700 -%}{%- assign fit = ' _fit' -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- if a.image and a.image.aspect_ratio >= 2.0 -%}{%- assign fit = ' _fit' -%}{%- endif -%}
 <div class="_shot{{ fit }}">
 {%- if a.image -%}
 <img src="{{ a.image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
 srcset="{{ a.image | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w, {{ a.image | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ a.image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
 sizes="(max-width:1199px) 100vw, 52vw"
 width="1200" height="750" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"
 alt="{{ a.image.alt | default: a.title | escape }}">
 {%- else -%}
 <div class="_ph" data-ph="{{ bitc_blog.title | escape }}"></div>
 {%- endif -%}
 {%- assign tg = a.tags | first -%}
 {%- if tg != blank -%}{%- comment -%}
 Store tags are namespaced (`cat:materials`). The namespace is stripped and the
 rest is looked up in the localized label list; an unknown tag falls back to its
 own text, so a new category never renders as a broken key.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- assign lbl_raw = tg | remove_first: 'cat:' | remove_first: 'CAT:' | strip -%}
 {%- assign lbl_h = lbl_raw | handle -%}
 {%- assign lbl = lbl_raw -%}
 {%- assign cat_keys = CATK | split: ',' -%}
 {%- assign cat_vals = t_catv | split: '|' -%}
 {%- for ck in cat_keys -%}
 {%- if ck == lbl_h -%}{%- assign lbl = cat_vals[forloop.index0] -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
 {%- endfor -%}<span class="_chip">#{{ lbl }}</span>{%- endif -%}
 {%- if ep_vid != blank -%}
 <span class="_play"><svg width="10" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 12" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 0l10 6-10 6z"/></svg> {{ t_video }}</span>
 {%- endif -%}
 </div>
 {%- if ep_no != blank -%}<p class="_ep _eyebrow"><b>{{ t_episode }} {{ ep_no }}</b></p>{%- endif -%}
 <h3 class="_h">{{ a.title }}</h3>
 {%- if a.excerpt_or_content != blank -%}
 <p class="_deck">{{ a.excerpt_or_content | strip_html | truncate: 185 }}</p>
 {%- endif -%}
 <div class="_foot">
 <span class="_meta">
 <time datetime="{{ a.published_at | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">{{ a.published_at | date: t_datefmt }}</time>
 {%- if SHOW_READ_TIME and ep_rt > 0 -%}<i class="_bar"></i><span>{{ ep_rt }} {{ t_read }}</span>{%- endif -%}
 </span>
 <span class="_more">{{ t_readmore }} <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 15 15" fill="none"><path d="M2.5 7.5h10M8.5 3.5l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
 </div>
 </a>
 </article>
 <div class="_list">
 {%- else -%}
 <a class="_row _lk" href="{{ a.url }}">
